# ============================================================
#  VampireHosting — Environment Variables Reference
# ============================================================
#
#  DO NOT put real keys in this file.
#  This file is just documentation / a template.
#
# ── Cloudflare Worker Secret (PRODUCTION) ────────────────────
#
#  The Gemini API key is stored as a Cloudflare encrypted secret.
#  It is injected into the Worker as env.GEMINI_API_KEY at runtime.
#  It is NEVER in source code, wrangler.toml, or git history.
#
#  To add/update the key:
#
#    npx wrangler secret put GEMINI_API_KEY
#    > Paste your key when prompted (from https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey)
#
#  To verify it exists (without revealing the value):
#
#    npx wrangler secret list
#
# ── CLI Usage on VPS ─────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  On your private VPS, the vampire AI command uses:
#
#    export GEMINI_API_KEY="your-key-here"
#    sudo -E vampire ai "How do I set up FiveM?"
#
#  OR it prompts you and saves to /etc/vampire/gemini.key (mode 600)
#
# ── Local Dev Only (NOT for production) ──────────────────────
#
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here_for_local_dev_only
